.TH mouser-show 1  "mouser-show 1.4.4" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mouser\-show \- Show images in this terminal (Fuzzball graphics, or Kitty graphics as a fallback; works in tmux with allow\-passthrough)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser show\fR [\fB\-\-width\fR] [\fB\-\-height\fR] [\fB\-\-fit\fR] [\fB\-\-original\fR] [\fB\-\-id\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILES\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show images in this terminal (Fuzzball graphics, or Kitty graphics as a fallback; works in tmux with allow\-passthrough).
.PP
Formats: PNG, JPEG, GIF (first frame), WebP, BMP. Video and audio are not supported. Works in Mouser, other Fuzzball terminals and Kitty\-graphics terminals; inside tmux it uses Kitty Unicode placeholders.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<WIDTH>\fR
Width in cells (height follows the aspect ratio)
.TP
\fB\-\-height\fR \fI<HEIGHT>\fR
Height in cells (width follows the aspect ratio)
.TP
\fB\-\-fit\fR
Fit the terminal width (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-original\fR
Natural size: one image pixel per screen pixel (the terminal still fits it to the screen)
.TP
\fB\-\-id\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Image id to use (default: derived from the process id)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILES\fR>
Image files; `\-` reads stdin. Shown one after another
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
